  "coupling_notes": [
    "Era arithmetic (days_from_civil/civil_from_days) couples to weekday computation through the days-from-epoch representation shared by date::year_month_day::to_days and date::weekday::weekday_from_days.",
    "ISO week encoding couples to Weekday::iso_encoding through the 0-to-7 Sunday re-encoding (iso_week::weekday::weekday_from_days agrees with date::weekday::iso_encoding for every z).",
    "All five obligations require creusot-deductive-check evidence; the promoted interactions' trust policy allows no assumptions, so trusted_assumptions is empty.",
    "gate_integrity entries for scripts/witness_renderer.py and scripts/xml_escape.py carry the real sha256 of the ligature-managed witness renderer and its direct helper as installed by ligature 1.1+ init/migrate; the ligature 1.0-era placeholder zero hashes are gone and G13 verifies these two hashes against the installed files.",
    "provenance.artifact_set_hash is the sha256 of the Stage 4.5 promotion receipt file specs/_promotions/date-creusot-core.json, the machine-readable record of the accepted artifact set."
  ],
